   245	To show that $\SMP(\A_{\M})$ is at least as hard as $\SMP(\A)$, we must reduce an instance of $\SMP(\A)$ to an instance of $\SMP(\A_{\M})$ in polynomial time such that the $\SMP(\A)$ instance has a `yes' answer if and only if the $\SMP(\A_{\M})$ instance has a `yes' answer. 
