   396	(ii) Let $\B$ be the finite algebra of Kozik \cite{Koz} for which the problem $\SMP(\B)$ is EXPTIME-complete. Then by statement (i) of the theorem, there exists a finite algebra $\B_\M$ such that $\B_\M \models \Sigma$ and $\SMP(\B_\M)$ is at least as hard as $\SMP(\B)$. Since the subpower membership problem can always be answered in EXPTIME, it follows that $\SMP(\B_\M)$ is EXPTIME-complete.
